  "$comment": [
    "CW Frogger (#190, part of #170), pinned for both ports: FroggerGame in",
    "ios/Sources/MorseKit/Frogger.swift and android/.../morsekit/Frogger.kt. Read by",
    "ios/Sources/MorseKitCheck/main.swift and android/app/src/test/.../morsekit/FroggerTest.kt.",
    "",
    "Every expected value below was worked out from the rules in 'derivation'",
    "by a script that knows only those rules, not captured from either port.",
    "Do not regenerate it to make a failing test pass; change it only when the",
    "rule is meant to change."
  ],
  "derivation": {
    "rules": [
      "The board has 9 rows: 0 is the start bank, 1-3 road lanes, 4 the median,",
      "5-7 river lanes, 8 the goal bank. Positions are normalised: x runs 0..1",
      "across the board and wraps. Each lane holds 'count' objects centred at",
      "(i + 0.5) / count when the lane is laid out (a new game and every new",
      "wave), moving 'direction' at laneSpeed and wrapping; an object that",
      "wraps 'enters' the board again.",
      "  laneSpeed = min(maxLaneSpeed, baseSpeed * waveSpeedGrowth^(wave-1)) / difficulty.timeScale",
      "The frog hops one row up or down, or 1/columns sideways, clamped so its",
      "centre stays within half a hop of the edges; a hop that moves it by less",
      "than 1e-9 (nothing, or only float noise at the clamp) is",
      "ignored. Every object carries a character from the learner's pool. Each",
      "lane gets a cue - one of the characters its objects carry - the first",
      "time the frog lands on the row below it in a crossing; the cue is what",
      "the game sends in Morse. On a road lane a vehicle carrying the cue is",
      "harmless and passing through it is a correct decision; touching any",
      "other vehicle is a wrong one (life lost). Road contact: wrapped |dx| <",
      "width/2 + frogHalfWidth, checked on every hop and every advance; a",
      "vehicle is credited once per overlap. On a river lane the frog must",
      "land with its centre over a log (wrapped |dx| < width/2): a cue log is",
      "a correct decision and carries the frog with it, any other log sinks,",
      "no log drowns (wrong, no confusion partner). A death costs a life and",
      "the combo, steps the speed ramp back, returns the frog to the start",
      "bank and clears every cue. Zero lives ends the game.",
      "Scoring: pointsPerHop for each hop onto a row higher than any reached",
      "in this crossing; pointsPerDecision x multiplier(combo) for a correct",
      "decision, where combo counts consecutive correct decisions and",
      "multiplier = min(4, 1 + (combo-1) div 3); pointsPerCrossing on reaching",
      "the goal, which also starts the next wave: lanes are laid out afresh at",
      "the new wave's speeds, the frog returns to the start bank, the combo",
      "is kept. Labels: waves 1-2 always shown ('visible'); waves 3-4 a lane's",
      "labels hide once it has been cued ('memory'); from wave 5 labels are",
      "never shown and objects announce their own character in Morse as they",
      "enter ('hidden').",
      "Speed ramp: a game opens rampStartOffset WPM under the character speed,",
      "never under minWpm; every decisionsPerStep correct decisions in total",
      "step it up rampStep WPM, capped at the character speed; a death steps",
      "it down rampStep, never under the start. bestWpm is the highest reached."
    ],
    "rows": 9,
    "startRow": 0,
    "medianRow": 4,
    "goalRow": 8,
    "columns": 7,
    "frogHalfWidth": 0.04,
    "waveSpeedGrowth": 1.08,
    "maxLaneSpeed": 0.5,
    "pointsPerHop": 10,
    "pointsPerDecision": 50,
    "pointsPerCrossing": 200,
    "memoryFromWave": 3,
    "hiddenFromWave": 5,
    "minWpm": 15,
    "rampStartOffset": 8,
    "rampStep": 2,
    "decisionsPerStep": 4
  },
